        {
            "_id": "QigLM8qDfI4HCzVz",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
            "name": "Echo the Past",
            "sort": 1200000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>The primordial echo calls forth a remnant of the past civilization to impart a lesson or control the present. Using this ability again ends any previous manifestation. The primordial echo casts one of the following occult innate spells (DC 38) for the listed purpose.</p>\n<p><em><strong>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Dominate]</strong></em> The dominated creature takes on the role of a historical figure or someone in the social hierarchy (such as high priest) from the primordial echo's civilization.</p>\n<p><em><strong>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Illusory Scene]</strong></em> The scene reenacts a historical event from the primordial echo's civilization.</p>\n<p><em><strong>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Invoke Spirits]</strong></em> The spirits are drawn from the primordial echo's memories of people from their civilization.</p>\n<p><em><strong>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Wall of Stone]</strong></em> The primordial echo recreates the wall of a building from their civilization, complete with decorations.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
